  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (2''s,3''s)-Epoxyangeloyldecursinol and the cancer cell line SCCH-26, through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of Interiorin, and Interiorin further targets SCCH-26. Similarly, the compound is also a target of CID 20842, which also targets SCCH-26. Additionally, the compound is linked to 5,7-dimethoxy-8-[(E)-3-oxobut-1-enyl]chromen-2-one, which also targets SCCH-26. These findings indicate that (2''s,3''s)-Epoxyangeloyldecursinol may exert its biological effects through multiple downstream pathways, ultimately influencing SCCH-26. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible role in modulating cellular processes that could contribute to the suppression of SCCH-26. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are similar across the different paths, but the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
